{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause: 463739cdb48 (2026-07-03) added the first-run seed from /opt/rebar/.deployed_ref with only a resolvability check. Nothing in the repo or on the host writes the marker (host grep: only autodeploy.sh references it); rsync excludes it. Host read-only 2026-11-04: deployed-sha = mcp-deployed-sha = bot-deployed-sha = 4496e9acd2a; marker d4a0a2a44 resolves in the mirror but merge-base --is-ancestor origin/main rc=1. Fix pushed as Gerrit 3298: seed only from a main ancestor, else adopt the tip and emit AUTODEPLOY_ERROR deployed-ref-off-main. Tests: tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_first_run_seed.py, off-main case failed before the fix (seeded the side commit) and passes after; 156/156 autodeploy tests, make lint, make typecheck green.\n\nOPERATOR STEP (not performed; production is read-only for agents): remove the stale marker on i-00880b2c7f13527c5 so the next state loss cannot even raise the deployed-ref-off-main signal:\n  sudo rm /opt/rebar/.deployed_ref\nSafe on the current host: steady state never reads it (deployed-sha is populated), and the fixed script refuses it anyway."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793791786760364001,"uuid":"f2485a02-cbfc-4edf-b18d-cc1a1fc9765f"}